.TH IMAGEEDITOR 1 "September 2026" "Vulkana Image Editor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
imageeditor \- Vulkana Image Editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imageeditor
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ document ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Linux image editor with a Vulkan canvas, editable raster, text and shape
layers, brushes and selections. Local .vulkana projects and raster images
open in document tabs. PSD files open a conversion review for editable layers,
text, simple shapes, masks and supported effects, with explicit raster fallbacks.
PDF files open the page import dialog. Without a document, the New Document dialog opens.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show command-line usage.
.TP
.B --version
Show the application version, independent of the native project schema.
.TP
.B --fps
Show the actual event-driven Vulkan canvas frame rate.
.TP
.BI --ui-config " path"
Read custom panel size defaults from an INI file once at startup.
.TP
.B --skip-new-dialog
Start a default transparent canvas without the startup prompt.
.TP
.B --force-update-check
Check for updates at startup. This is now the default; the flag is retained
for compatibility. No update is downloaded without user action.
.TP
.B --test-update
Show a simulated newer release in the normal update notice and About panel.
Works offline without service configuration. Downloads and AppImage replacement
are disabled. Close any running instance before launching with this flag.
.TP
.B --smoke-test
Run automated lifecycle checks and exit. This diagnostic requires the
optional Khronos Vulkan validation layer; normal editing does not.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vulkanaEditor/vulkanaEditor.conf
Preferences, recent files and panel layout.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/vulkanaEditor/brush-presets-v2
Custom brush preset copies. Packaged presets are immutable.
.TP
.I /usr/share/vulkana-editor
Read-only shaders, assets and layout defaults.
.PP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME and XDG_DATA_HOME override the corresponding user roots.
Projects are saved at the user's chosen location.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B IMAGEEDITOR_UI_CONFIG
is an optional alternative to --ui-config. No development environment
variables are needed for installed operation.
.SH NOTES
Wayland and X11 are supported. A working Vulkan 1.2 driver is required.
Vulkana-owned code and assets use the MIT License. Third-party components
